277 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 202 0 R
/E ( FTC Team 17315 originates from Westwood High School in Austin, Texas. In 2020, Team 17315 became the 3rd addition to the Westwood Robotics Organization, which now encompasses a total of four teams. Team 17315 has been participating in FIRST for a total of five years )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
278 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 202 0 R
/E (  This year, the team is composed of fourteen high school students \(three juniors, seven sophomores, and four freshmen\), with a rookie to veteran ratio of 4:10.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
279 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 202 0 R
/E (Each member specializes in one of four subcategories \(three marketing, four software, three outreach, and three hardware\), but all members are highly encouraged to contribute to every aspect of the team.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
280 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 202 0 R
/E ( This helps foster a healthy learning environment and enables us to approach problems from multi-faceted viewpoints. Team members are committed to inspiring excellence in our peers and spreading the core values of FIRST within the community and around the world.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
281 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 202 0 R
/T (Team Motto)
/E (Team Motto)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
282 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 202 0 R
/E ("To Forge Our Path" embodies Tomahawk's dedication to using purpose, perseverance, and unwavering effort to shape our own success. Every member of Team 17315 is molded by the effort we put into our designs, outreach, and community, just as a tomahawk must be forged with heat, pressure, and precision. Tomahawk never waits for opportunities; instead, we create them, as evidenced by the concept of "forging our path". We take on seemingly insurmountable challenges, surpass expectations, and emerge stronger, more capable, and sharper. We work with purpose and impact, whether we're developing FIRST in our community, mentoring less experienced teams, or engineering in the workshop. It represents our conviction that excellence is developed, honed, and earned rather than accidental. And in the process, we leave a legacy that encourages others to embrace FIRST.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
