348 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 206 0 R
/T (Our type of leadership and communication was heavily inspired from the Boy Scouts PLC System. In the Boy Scouts PLC system, student troop leaders will speak together monthly with adult leaders in attendance. The most important part of the PLC system is that adult leaders do NOT lead the discussions, rather let the student leaders discuss their issues and only intervene when they deem it is needed. Similarly, in our meetings adult mentors are simply there to observe and give suggestions where they feel it is necessary. This allows the team to be student driven and makes our passion for FTC greater. Also in the PLC Meeting, Troop\(Boy Scout\) Members are allowed to request an issue to be brought up at the meetings to anyone on the leadership crew. If they feel they themselves need to bring up the issue, the Scout is welcome to attend. Similarly, we have a system where a team member can request a topic to be brought up or may attend the leadership meetings we hold monthly and discuss it with us. )
/E (Our type of leadership and communication was heavily inspired from the Boy Scouts PLC System. In the Boy Scouts PLC system, student troop leaders will speak together monthly with adult leaders in attendance. The most important part of the PLC system is that adult leaders do NOT lead the discussions, rather let the student leaders discuss their issues and only intervene when they deem it is needed. Similarly, in our meetings adult mentors are simply there to observe and give suggestions where they feel it is necessary. This allows the team to be student driven and makes our passion for FTC greater. Also in the PLC Meeting, Troop\(Boy Scout\) Members are allowed to request an issue to be brought up at the meetings to anyone on the leadership crew. If they feel they themselves need to bring up the issue, the Scout is welcome to attend. Similarly, we have a system where a team member can request a topic to be brought up or may attend the leadership meetings we hold monthly and discuss it with us. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
